# Delivery loop

The master copy is `conduct/methodology/SKILL.md`, versioned by git tags. Clients pin a tag and add overlays. Code conduct is `conduct/conduct/SKILL.md`. Conduct stays in that skill.

The engine is the only status writer. Workers leave tracker calls to the engine.

The orchestrator talks to the owner. The engineering bot owns the code and runs the loop: it dispatches sweeps, launches cloud agents, and merges, or leaves the merge to the lander or the engine-heal workflow. Any actor may squash-merge once quality is green on the head. GitHub is the record.

Sweep reads `status.intake` (default Todo). One runner holds the ticket with a `DELIVERY_LEASE` comment and records the live agent id as soon as the worker starts. Ground, then build, then one pull request per land repo. Quality is green before the squash. A branch that is only behind is updated from trunk, then quality runs again on the new head. Trunk quality is green before `dev.promote` and before the dev status. `dev.promote` runs only for repos listed in `dev.promote.repos`. Ship is a separate command unless `ship.afterDev` is set. A failed ship step leaves the dev status.

A required step that returned no has one heal: edit, wait, or login. edit changes the owner of the failure. When that owner is this package, open branch `engine-heal/<ticket>`, label it `engine-heal`, and include the next patch after the highest `v*` tag. The `pull_request` `quality` check gates it. The workflow squash-merges that head and may tag the merge commit. A pull request without the bump gets a comment and stops. A client pins the tag when it needs the change.

Heal caps live in `delivery-loop.yaml` under `heal.maxAttempts` and `heal.caps`. The default is 3 per failure type (`quality-red`, `merge-conflict`, `promote-failed`, `ship-failed`, `quality-pending`, `quality-unscheduled`, `runner-blocked`, `other`). The count is `OWNER_HEAL` comments on the ticket. At the cap the engine labels `heal-exhausted` and the failure type, writes `HEAL_EXHAUSTED`, and stops. A failed marker comment fails the heal.

Token and secret values are never printed or stored.
